resources.string:
"【Principle】Watermark attacks weaken or destroy the watermark via signal processing or geometric transforms (Ch. 8, 8.5):
① Simple attacks: JPEG compression (Ch. 5 quantization), noise, filtering — only attenuate watermark energy;
② Synchronization attacks: scaling/rotation/cropping — break the spatial synchronization between watermark and cover;
③ Frame dropping: specific to video, breaks temporal synchronization.
【Eq. 8-6】NC = Σ(w·w′) / (√Σw² · √Σw′²), correlation between extracted and original watermark;
【Eq. 8-7】BER = erroneous bits / total bits × 100%;
PSNR reflects attack strength (lower means more severe).
【General countermeasures】Redundant embedding + majority voting, error-correcting codes, larger embedding strength, synchronization templates, inter-frame redundancy."
